# 🧠 Image Classifier using TensorFlow

This project is a simple deep learning-based image classification model built using **TensorFlow** and **Keras**. It classifies images into predefined categories using a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN).

## 🚀 Features

- Built with TensorFlow and Keras
- Uses CNN architecture for high accuracy
- Trained on a custom dataset
- Capable of classifying images into different categories
- Easy to train and test with new images

## 🧾 Requirements

- Python 3.x  
- TensorFlow  
- NumPy  
- Matplotlib  
- scikit-learn  

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## 🛠 How to Run

1. Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/Image_Classification_CNN_using_tensorflow.git
```

2. Navigate into the project folder:

```bash
cd Image_Classification_CNN_using_tensorflow
```

3. Train the model:

```bash
python train.py
```

4. Test the model with new images:
download any one of the feature images ie horse, truck, airplane etc

Make sure to crop it into a 32 x 32 format and save it as jpg

follow this procedure to load your image and use the saved model to predict what image it is, 
example: 

## Loading the our images to make predictions
img = cv.imread("truck.jpg")

## Prediction
##NB divide the image by 255 to scale it to 0-1 as we did on the training data
prediction = model.predict(np.array([img])/255)

## Use argmax to select the index of the neuron with the highest probability
index = np.argmax([prediction])
print(f"Prediction is : {class_names[index]}")

